 :the-carrier-measurement
 ;; The one measurement that decided how the rest of the component is written.
 {:question
  "amu check admits :document, which the skill and amu's own todo-app.kotoba
   name as the idiomatic carrier for heterogeneous data. Does the target this
   component must RUN on admit it?"
  :answer :no
  :probe "q9-probes/p17-native-carrier.kotoba"
  :check-exit 0
  :native-exit 70
  :native-message
  "typed values currently require the kotoba-script web target, typed Wasm
   target, or qualified native string/scalar-record/option-i64/result-i64
   features"
  :control-that-makes-it-a-measurement
  "The same pair of verdicts holds for amu's own two reference applications,
   in opposite directions: examples/todo-app.kotoba (document carrier)
   compiles for no native target, examples/approval-queue-app.kotoba (string
   carrier) compiles for aarch64-macos. So the refusal is the carrier's and
   not this component's."
  :what-follows
  "The rows cross as JSON text, the way approval-queue-app's state does. For a
   REST actor that is the wire format the component already speaks, so it is
   not a reshaping of the domain to dodge the gap -- but it IS a gap, and a
   :document-carried version of this component would pass check and produce no
   artifact to run."
  :other-heads-check-admits-and-native-refuses
  "string-fold-case (str/lower), string-split-count (str/split), :f64 with
   decimal-f64-parse (as-float), typed maps of every key/value pair tried,
   typed sets of :string, and `min` -- the last three of those under a
   different message, `aggregate ABI rejected: call-abi-not-admitted`, which
   also covers string-contains? and string-index-of. Probe:
   q9-probes/p18-native-refusals.kotoba. typed sets of :keyword, string-join,
   string-replace-all, string-from-i64, keyword-from-string, keyword-name and
   [:option :string] all DO reach native."}

 :the-trap-that-was-fuel
 ;; A refusal that was one command away from being written down as a language
 ;; finding, in the exact shape ADR-2609081600 names.
 {:symptom
  "The store, filter, handler and healthz oracles all answered KEXE_TRAP
   {:kind :signal :signal :SIGTRAP}, exit 120, on the aarch64 artifact, while
   the shorter-string oracles beside them answered normally. `oracle-table 0`
   trapped and `oracle-table 1,2,3` did not; the only difference between them
   is that ReserveData's field list is a 240-byte literal."
  :two-hypotheses-both-false
  "A string-length ceiling and a recursion-depth ceiling. Both were measured
   and both are false: 256 appends (depth 256, length 256) answers 256, and
   10 doublings (depth 10, length 1024) answers 1024. Probe:
   q9-probes/p24-fuel-is-not-the-language.kotoba."
  :actual-cause
  "tools/kexe_loader.c: `static uint64_t kexe_initial_fuel = 512;` unless
   KEXE_FUEL names another budget. Fuel is charged per function ENTRY, and a
   scan that enters a function per byte of a 240-byte literal spends it."
  :verification
  "With KEXE_FUEL=100000000 every trapping oracle answers, and answers the
   same number aave.main answers. Nothing in the component changed."
  :why-it-is-recorded
  "Had it been written down as measured, this file would say the store layer
   is blocked on the native backend, and nine other repos in this family would
   have inherited that. The loader's default budget is not the language."
  :and-it-bit-a-second-time-within-the-hour
  "Reproducing the above independently, every oracle kept trapping WITH
   KEXE_FUEL raised, and `KEXE_STRUCTURED_REPORT=1` said why: `:fuel {:initial
   512 :remaining 0}` -- the budget was never applied. The loader binary had
   been built from tools/kexe_loader.c in the SHARED checkout
   orgs/kotoba-lang/amu, which sits on a local cron-tick commit and contains
   the string KEXE_FUEL zero times; at amu's pin it appears three times.
   Rebuilt from the pin, the same call answers `:status :ok :result 201`.
   Same error class as :the-internal-compiler-error-was-mine and as the
   jvm-surface detector's amu finding, three times in one session: a number
   read off a tree that is not the one being reasoned about. The detector now
   marks its own instance of it (root 3bef1bf6); nothing marks this one except
   this sentence."
  :independent-rerun
  "14 of 14 oracle-handlers selectors agree with aave.main once the loader is
   built from the pin: 201/400/400/200/200/404/200/404/200/404/1/3/2/99. The
   two 400s are correct and my first table was wrong -- fixture 1 omits a
   :required field and fixture 2 carries an unknown one, so require-fields and
   reject-unknown are supposed to answer 400. main answers 20, which is
   aave.main/routes' length (4 entities x 5 routes)."}

