 {:entity-specs
  {:status :ported
   :evidence
   "oracle-table 0..3 against the joined entity|plural|id-prefix|fields|
    required|coerce line built from aave.main/entity-specs. 1, 2 and 3 are
    hash-equal. 0 is not, and the difference is entirely the ITERATION ORDER
    of ReserveData's 9-entry :coerce map, which Clojure makes a hash map at
    that size: measured set-equal (9 pairs both sides), while :fields and
    :required -- which are vectors and genuinely ordered -- are string-equal.
    :coerce is only ever read with (get coerce f), so its order is not
    semantic."}
  :routes
  {:status :ported
   :evidence
   "oracle-route-shape 0..19 against (str/join \" \" [method path (str op
