  :now
  {:status :ported-with-a-stub-clock
   :evidence
   "The clock crosses as the declared capability import :clock/now (wire 7)
    and the call traps when the grant is withdrawn. The RFC-3339 rendering --
    Howard Hinnant's civil_from_days in i64 arithmetic plus string-from-i64,
    because Kotoba has no date library -- was checked against an independent
    oracle, (.toISOString (js/Date. (* 1000 secs))) with the milliseconds
    removed, at epochs 0, 1, 1000000000 and 1757000000. All four hashes equal."
   :what-is-not-real
   "The number the clock capability answers under tools/kexe_loader.c is NOT a
    wall clock. Measured: (clock/now s) answers s+1 for s in 0,1,2,10, so
    (now s) renders the instant s+1 seconds after the epoch. kexe_loader.c's
    hosted_clock_v1 wants a structured request (an ordinal and a payload
    packed into the i64) which this component does not construct, so the call
    takes the echo path. The capability is wired and the arithmetic is
    verified; the input is a stub."}
  :new-id
  {:status :ported
